# Withdrawing from the game (GAME-09, docs/m6-plan.md M6.2; zero-vtes rules-qa Batch 95). With an
# empty library and less than a full hand, a Methuselah announces it in their unlock phase. If by
# their next unlock phase they lose or spend no pool or blood and none of their minions enters
# combat, they leave the game with half a VP: not an oust, so nobody is rewarded.
seed 16
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
# Small libraries: the opening draw empties them, leaving 5 cards in hand.
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *8
library A "Iron Ward" *5
crypt B "Tomas Grey" *8
library B "Signal Fire" *5
crypt C "Ilse Várga" *8
library C "Quick Feed" *20
start
expect turn 1 A unlock
expect count A:library 0
expect count A:hand 5

# Alice withdraws, and plays her turn as usual.
A> withdraw
expect withdrawing A yes
log public A announces a withdrawal: they leave the game at the start of their next turn, if they lose or spend no pool or blood and none of their minions enters combat
reject:no-change A> withdraw
A> next
# Only in your own unlock phase.
reject:not-now B> withdraw
A> next
A> next
A> next
A> next
expect turn 2 B unlock
B> next
B> next
B> next
B> next
B> next
expect turn 3 C unlock
# Carol still has cards in her library.
reject:not-now C> withdraw
C> next
C> next
C> next
C> next
C> next
# Alice's turn would start: her withdrawal held, so she leaves with ½ VP and Bob plays.
expect withdrawn A yes
expect vp A 0.5
expect vp C 0
expect status active
expect turn 4 B unlock
log public A withdrew from the game (+½ VP)

# Bob withdraws, then loses pool by his own hand: it no longer holds. He may announce it again
# while the conditions hold, but spending pool in his influence phase nullifies it again.
B> withdraw
B> pool -1
expect withdrawing B no
log public B's withdrawal no longer holds: they lost or spent pool
B> withdraw
B> next
B> next
B> next
B> transfer +1 B:uncontrolled:1
expect withdrawing B no
B> next
B> next
expect turn 5 C unlock
C> next
C> next
C> next
C> next
C> next

# This time it holds: Bob leaves, Carol is the last Methuselah standing, and the game is over.
expect turn 6 B unlock
B> withdraw
B> next
B> next
B> next
B> next
B> next
expect turn 7 C unlock
C> next
C> next
C> next
C> next
C> next
expect withdrawn B yes
expect status finished
expect ended last-standing
expect vp C 1
expect winner C
expect gamewin none
